  message: "Merged in PR #1417 (dev c5249c1aa1).\n\nFixed on jgstern-agent/fix/mulul-catalogue-rows (2a02346d00): rust.yaml std::process [exit, abort] and the same-shape elixir.yaml System.halt removed from subprocess; their HIGH_RISK_EXEMPTIONS_SUBPROCESS entries removed; a reverse guard now requires every exemption to name a live subprocess row. Behavioral evidence (one-file rust fixture, env::var -> process::exit): before, \"never launches a subprocess\" and host_secret->subprocess were VIOLATED and other claims were withheld with \"the analysis launches an external program at 2 call site(s) (std::process.abort, std::process.exit)\"; after, both read INCONCLUSIVE (unclassified call into std::process) and no verdict says a program was launched. Production-path test: test_process_exit_is_not_a_subprocess.py::test_an_exit_fed_from_the_environment_is_not_a_launch[rust,elixir]. Corpus: netavark's 4 std::process.exit subprocess chains are gone. NOT asserted: a CONFIRMED verdict over an exit call -- that needs a std::process completeness grant, blocked on the pid ruling (WI-kizur). Same-family residuals: WI-livod (swift fatalError family, erlang exit/1)."  # 3161
